# Cloudflare static-asset headers (Workers Assets honours this file, as Pages does).
#
# The Windows download has a FIXED filename so its URL can be linked from elsewhere,
# which means freshness cannot come from a versioned path. Installed clients poll
# ContentHub-Native.exe.md5 to notice a new build, so neither the sidecar nor the binary
# may sit in a long-lived cache — a stale .md5 makes clients blind to an update, and a
# stale .exe makes them download a build whose hash does not match.
#
# Five minutes: long enough to absorb a burst of downloads, short enough that a new
# build is picked up promptly. Both files use the SAME max-age on purpose, so the pair
# can never be served from different generations.
/download/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
